      "judgment_rationale": "OAuthCallback is a production Web route that validates provider, code, and state inputs, exchanges them through POST /api/v1/auth/oauth/{provider}/callback, accepts only a strict bearer/user/same-origin redirect response, updates authenticated state, and resumes the returned route. The d91 backend owns one-time expiring state and provider exchange authority rather than returning HTTP 501. Desktop has no audited native callback/deep-link route, so Cloud remains planned and Local Cloud-identity callback semantics are not applicable."
