      "expected_observable_result": "Cloud Desktop restores the native #/invite?token= deep link without placing the opaque token in route scope or logs; verifies anonymously through GET /api/v1/invitations/verify/{token}; preserves the hash across native sign-in; accepts through authenticated POST /api/v1/invitations/accept/{token}; refreshes the authoritative tenant catalog; and exposes structured invalid, expired, forbidden, conflict, unavailable, and retry states. Local Desktop returns local_tenant_invitation_not_applicable before module loading or fetch.",
      "judgment_rationale": "InviteAccept is a production-only Web route backed by public verify and authenticated accept operations. Cloud Desktop now owns a native global /invite route with the opaque token isolated in one bounded query parameter, anonymous verification without an Authorization header, authenticated acceptance using the current vault-backed session after sign-in, strict response contracts, abortable requests, explicit email-mismatch and expiry presentation, and an authoritative post-accept tenant-catalog refresh. The Desktop query-form path is an intentional native security deviation from Web /invite/:token: it keeps the credential-like token out of DesktopRouteContext, capability scope, breadcrumb identity, and permission audit fields while preserving the hash across sign-in. Local mode does not reproduce multi-user organization membership and fails closed with local_tenant_invitation_not_applicable."
